<include>
    <!--
        priority in which codecs are applied

        1 - absolute_codec, if set it will use that value
        2.1 - if media_mix_inbound_outbound_codecs is set then originator codecs + outbound_codecs are offered
        2.2 - if media_mix_inbound_outbound_codecs is NOT set then only the inbound codecs are offered, this prevents transcoding
    -->

    <!--
        this is the setting to prevent transcoding bypass

        this was enabled as devices with empty codec list 
        were only offered the originator codec
        to prevent transcoding.
        this settings will make freeswitch offer the originator codec
        plus the outbound_codecs list.
         
        the sdp payload gets very large when enabled
        specially for inbound webrtc calls to sip devices
    -->
    <X-PRE-PROCESS cmd="set" data="media_mix_inbound_outbound_codecs=true"/>

    <!-- deprecating single setting for inbound/outbound -->
    <X-PRE-PROCESS cmd="set" data="codecs=PCMU,AMR-WB,AMR,OPUS,G723,G7231,G726-16,G726-40,G7221@32000h,G7221@16000h,G722,PCMA,VP8,H264"/>


    <!--
        having inbound_codecs and outbound_codecs separately
        allows to only send a small codec list for outbound calls when
        the endpoint codec list is empty

        inbound_codecs is the priority list: the profile negotiates
        greedy, so a caller's leg takes the first of these it offers, and
        a callee is offered the caller's codecs in this order. G722 first
        keeps calls between our phones and apps wideband, and Telnyx's
        HD Voice turns AMR-WB mobile calls into G722 for us; anything
        else falls back to G.711.

        list only codecs this build can encode and decode. A codec that
        is only passed through (AMR and G723 without their libraries;
        AMR-WB and G7221 are not built at all) leaves a call silent once
        its other leg, after a transfer say, takes something else.

        outbound_codecs follow the caller's codecs in an offer, and are
        the whole offer for a leg with no caller (click-to-call, quickcall,
        originate).
    -->
    <X-PRE-PROCESS cmd="set" data="inbound_codecs=G722,PCMU,PCMA,OPUS,VP8,H264,VP9"/>
    <X-PRE-PROCESS cmd="set" data="outbound_codecs=G722,PCMU,PCMA"/>

    <!--
        the caller's leg takes the codec its callee answered with, when the
        caller offered it, rather than picking its own: late negotiation
        then ends with both legs on one codec and nothing transcoded.
        Bridges that set inherit_codec themselves (click-to-call,
        quickcall, doorman) keep their own value.
    -->
    <X-PRE-PROCESS cmd="set" data="inherit_codec=true"/>


</include>
